		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 167.64 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
		)
		(uuid "9a8c7e3a-e04e-4477-89c2-a60d16d07479")
	)
	(text "RJ45 pinout (CiA 303-1):\n 1  CAN_H          5  reserved (NC)\n 2  CAN_L          6  CAN_SHLD (not connected)\n 3  CAN_GND        7  CAN_GND\n 4  reserved (NC)  8  CAN_V+ (24 V)\n 9/10  connector shell tabs -> SHIELD"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.59 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a03b0ac1-97cb-42c0-bcde-e6d4ceeb8146")
	)
	(text "CAN Bus Ports"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.67 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a52a612b-f52f-418b-a78d-114ccaceea0c")
	)
	(text "Shield bond - single point.\nR109 straps it solid for EMC testing; fit R106||C100 OR R109, never both."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.59 141.99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a87bdf89-2ee2-4b25-89d1-3f9c1350fd97")
	)
	(text "Per port, in order from the RJ45 inwards:\n  D43-D48  PESD2CANFD27V  CAN-FD ESD array, SOT-23-3\n  L1-L6    51 uH CAN common-mode choke, 1812 (Coilcraft 1812CAN fp)\n  FB1-FB6  120 R @ 100 MHz, 2 A ferrite bead, 0603\n  C102-C107  100 nF 50 V, 0603\n\nPCB LAYOUT - daisy chain, not a star: route CANH/CANL as ONE linear trunk\nRJ7 -> RJ8 -> RJ9 -> RJ10 -> RJ11 -> RJ12, entering and leaving each\nconnector. Keep every connector stub under 5 mm and run CANH/CANL as a\ntight differential pair with CAN_GND alongside.\nPut D4x hard against its connector, then L, so surge is clamped before the\nchoke and common-mode current is stopped at the point it leaves the board.\nFB + C filter 24 V at the connector so CAN_V+ cannot carry noise down the\ncable. U17 on sheet 1 limits the SUM of all ports to 0.87 A, so each bead\nmust carry the full 0.87 A worst case.\n\nJ11-J16: fit a 2.54 mm shunt to feed CAN_V+ (24 V) to pin 8 of that port.\nPin 6 (CAN_SHLD) is left unconnected - only the shell tabs carry the shield.\n\nEMC: L1-L6, FB1-FB6 and R109 may be fitted as 0 R links / left off on the\nfirst build. Take a stuffed and an unstuffed board to pre-scan."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.14 123.19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d9e5c533-1d3c-4c36-9fdb-250a40956b37")
	)
